1774116775897414	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvCA		item.create	bn-xg3	{"description":"The headless `msh render` command auto-frames the camera based on mesh bounds,\nbut for sprite baking we need a fixed dimetric camera angle (e.g. eye at\n3.0,2.5,3.0 targeting 0.0,0.5,0.0).\n\nAdd:\n  --camera-pos x,y,z     Camera eye position\n  --camera-target x,y,z  Camera look-at target\n\nWhen provided, these override the auto-framing.","kind":"task","title":"msh render: add --camera-pos and --camera-target flags"}	blake3:rYSPolSZs4iwoXCTR8ZcGFiyh3SaSzTVp-9-SPDr0fI
1774116776062101	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvCQ		item.create	bn-2nr	{"description":"When using `msh render --preset sprite-bake` with a GLB that has per-material\ncolors (from Blender Principled BSDF), the preset's base_color overrides\nthe per-material colors and everything renders gray.\n\nExpected: the preset should set projection, shading, transparent bg, etc.\nbut NOT override base_color when the mesh has per-material colors.\n\nWorkaround: skip --preset and pass individual flags:\n  --projection ortho --ortho-height 3.5 --transparent-bg --shading flat","kind":"bug","title":"msh render: sprite-bake preset should not override per-material colors"}	blake3:TJIWKiCgPsZu2UPvkUpYVIPM9dSXCeCdY3T3pIAKCUg
