1774119386208110	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvCg		item.create	bn-1xv	{"description":"Same clap negative-number issue as the other flags. Camera positions with\nnegative coordinates fail:\n\n  msh render model.glb -o out.png --camera-pos -1.5,1.0,2.0\n  error: unexpected argument '-1' found\n\nWorkaround: use = form: --camera-pos=-1.5,1.0,2.0\n\nFix: add allow_negative_numbers or allow_hyphen_values to the clap arg.","kind":"bug","title":"msh render: --camera-pos and --camera-target reject negative values"}	blake3:ZYArwSUSXN2jKQ6fGZOP0TPRzF4uEbiOoz12O7bhFrE
1774136981397919	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvCw		item.create	bn-1u7	{"description":"When rendering with `msh render --preset sprite-bake --ortho-height`, the orthographic projection produces incorrect screen-space angles for ground-plane edges. A 30° camera elevation (sin(30°)=0.5) should produce ground-plane edges at exactly 2:1 pixel ratio, but instead produces ~2.19:1.\n\nMeasured empirically:\n- At 30° elevation (eye=[4.5, 3.674, 4.5], target=[0, 0.4, 0]): slope=0.456 (2.19:1)\n- Correct 2:1 slope required eye=[4.5, 4.112, 4.5] — found by binary search\n\nLikely cause: the look-at matrix or ortho projection matrix has an error in how the up vector or aspect ratio interacts with the elevation angle. In a correct ortho projection, sin(elevation)=0.5 should always yield 2:1 ground-plane edges.\n\nImpact: command-lattice sprite baking needs empirically calibrated camera Y values instead of clean theoretical formula.","kind":"bug","title":"ortho projection produces wrong dimetric angle"}	blake3:BlWjfh_YDGkbKj_euCF7VDOCuuSgJxzAvr-mVbk774g
1774137044601227	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtbQ		item.move	bn-1xv	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:BPrP0WG5BO4nX0wSB7LPpcUIWaR2fA1Mtz3ZbdH15X4
1774137044606367	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtbg		item.assign	bn-1xv	{"action":"assign","agent":"msh-dev"}	blake3:8M6pARTYi9o8lbIdsh2SMqr1XUpb2oTFjbHB5Oh5Pco
1774137044622799	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtbw		item.move	bn-1u7	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:t86Fxka3FtAAHQ1T1ZzHLeQImYEdxCHQrPfxydY0zTM
1774137044626851	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtcA		item.assign	bn-1u7	{"action":"assign","agent":"msh-dev"}	blake3:ZkTugkPeSCpXoZnc4PkaIT7A88RWReat1b6pjytt-xU
1774137172024358	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtcQ		item.update	bn-1u7	{"field":"description","value":"## Not a bug — target offset changes effective elevation\n\nThe ortho projection and look-at matrices are mathematically correct. The reported slope mismatch (0.456 instead of 0.5) is caused by the target Y offset.\n\nWith eye=(4.5, 3.674, 4.5) and target=(0, 0, 0): the direction is (4.5, 3.674, 4.5), giving sin(elevation) = 0.5000, slope = exactly 0.5 (2:1 ratio). Correct.\n\nWith target=(0, 0.4, 0): the direction becomes (4.5, 3.274, 4.5), giving sin(elevation) = 0.4575, slope = 0.4575 (2.19:1). This matches the reported measurement.\n\nFix for sprite baking: use target=(0, 0, 0) since the mesh is already centered at origin by the loader. Or adjust eye.y to compensate: eye.y = target.y + d * sin(elevation), where d = distance from eye to target."}	blake3:95A4bbmKrvSRdm0Jgb8sjVEDkqsRj3Zn7Dvlg5WveSE
1774137172042092	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtcg		item.move	bn-1u7	{"state":"done"}	blake3:LOAPNDb6orSvRHP7nKHHWykQCnsKVhKwLVReJmwliIw
1774137310090464	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtcw		item.move	bn-1xv	{"state":"done"}	blake3:SrEiH8htCGIATWLkCgmGY3baow5cWIFM2WubCWGD4m8
1774142507386219	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvDA		item.create	bn-1rv	{"description":"The msh viewer currently renders GLB meshes without materials — just plain geometry. When loading a GLB with embedded PBR materials (baseColorTexture, metallicRoughness), the viewer should sample and display the albedo texture mapped via the mesh's UV coordinates. This is needed to verify textured 3D assets generated by AI pipelines (e.g. TRELLIS) without requiring Blender.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- msh view model.glb renders the baseColorTexture on the mesh surface\n- UV coordinates (TEXCOORD_0) are read from the GLB and used for texture sampling\n- Optional: metallicRoughness texture support (can be a follow-up)","kind":"task","title":"Render GLB materials/textures in viewer"}	blake3:oamuOpakifmzncSc62cg9dNXjw60FBFgl5PEd2S0pKQ
1774144027835239	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtdA		item.move	bn-1rv	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:hm9x1Y3uOvtACVz-A2TVB6Fkrhk3VhmVsHHRcWPgjZY
