1774198618082558	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthAE		item.create	bn-1jm	{"description":"Investigate how the gltf crate (v1.4.1) exposes skin data: inverse bind matrices, joint hierarchy, joint indices/weights per vertex. Determine what accessor types are used and how to extract them. Check if the crate handles sparse accessors for joint data. Document the data flow from gltf::Skin → joint tree.","kind":"task","labels":["research"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"s","title":"Research: glTF skin/joint data in gltf crate"}	blake3:I5fZ-dfMtUIbKT2-OzEJMcUTFc0wO4nyh_iz3-LuIhA
1774198620674925	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthQE		item.create	bn-1sr	{"description":"Investigate how the gltf crate exposes animation data: channels, samplers, keyframe times, output values (translation/rotation/scale). Understand the three interpolation modes (Step, Linear, CubicSpline). Determine buffer layout for rotation quaternions vs translation vec3s. Check how multiple animations are indexed.","kind":"task","labels":["research"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"s","title":"Research: glTF animation channels and interpolation"}	blake3:k3g9zYWHdDo616bq3VvaYE_jodv90Na_gYl-1JzmgLo
1774198624154379	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthgE		item.create	bn-2jm	{"description":"Study the BVH file format: HIERARCHY section (joint names, offsets, channels) and MOTION section (frame time, channel data). Evaluate existing Rust BVH crates (bvh_anim, etc.) for suitability. Identify the key challenge: mapping BVH joint names/hierarchy to glTF skeleton joints for retargeting. Determine MVP scope — matching skeletons only, or basic name-based retargeting.","kind":"task","labels":["research"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"s","title":"Research: BVH format parsing and skeleton mapping"}	blake3:DIPInG-ZZCz7QhI0vOvwYHzrpvVQVY6OV24UBMBFsmI
1774198627544256	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthwE		item.create	bn-l2s	{"description":"Determine practical limits for joint palette uniforms in wgpu. A typical skeleton has 50-150 joints × 64 bytes (mat4) = 3.2-9.6 KB. Check maxUniformBufferBindingSize on common backends (Vulkan, Metal, DX12). Decide between uniform buffer vs storage buffer for the joint matrices. Check if the current bind group layout needs restructuring.","kind":"task","labels":["research"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"xs","title":"Research: wgpu uniform buffer limits for joint palettes"}	blake3:GCurJnOaqqiLIRscQ2lFp8SvfYhzhWI24YHDbl3Ud_0
1774198634204929	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtiAE		item.create	bn-30x	{"description":"Add joint_indices: [u32; 4] and joint_weights: [f32; 4] to the Vertex struct in mesh_renderer.rs. Update the vertex buffer layout (VertexBufferLayout, attributes, shader locations). Update extract_render_data() to propagate joint data through the triangle soup expansion. Default to zero weights for non-skinned meshes so the shader passthrough works.","kind":"task","labels":["skinning"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Extend Vertex struct with joint indices and weights"}	blake3:WpVdpi_qjLEpAHhlaw1Kjxe8yaIiiCtrY23KdFpio5c
1774198637736926	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtiQE		item.create	bn-1zv	{"description":"Extend load_mesh_with_colors() in loader.rs to extract: joint indices (JOINTS_0 accessor), joint weights (WEIGHTS_0 accessor), skin inverse bind matrices, and joint node hierarchy. Store in a new Skeleton struct with: joints (index, name, parent, inverse_bind_matrix) and per-vertex joint/weight data. Handle the case where a mesh has no skin (current behavior).","kind":"task","labels":["skinning"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Parse glTF skin data in loader"}	blake3:JkZV6BtaLtu_LPtTaT2hyW0fT7zYliUWb34PF9PqNMM
1774198641674353	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtigE		item.create	bn-1uc	{"description":"Implement joint hierarchy traversal: given a Skeleton, compute the world-space transform for each joint by walking parent→child. Compute final joint matrix = globalTransform × inverseBindMatrix for each joint. Produce a flat array of mat4 suitable for upload as a GPU uniform/storage buffer. Verify correctness: a skinned mesh in bind pose should look identical to the unskinned version.","kind":"task","labels":["skinning"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Build joint tree and compute bind-pose matrices"}	blake3:hOSppGL7LaVklfG40vLaPwGSkpuKZDJJksMVRPj6R2c
1774198645361261	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtiwE		item.create	bn-283	{"description":"Add a storage/uniform buffer for the joint palette (array of mat4, max ~256 joints). Create a new bind group or extend existing one. Update mesh.wgsl vertex shader to compute: skinned_pos = sum(weight[i] * joint_matrix[joint_index[i]] * position) for i in 0..4. Also skin normals (when we add them). Gate skinning on a uniform flag so non-skinned meshes still work.","kind":"task","labels":["skinning"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Add joint palette uniform and skinning shader"}	blake3:Q9DqXrzxD5gDv08IXsikdnWmmIihI4fyhw0Ums21bLY
1774198648813346	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjAE		item.create	bn-14n	{"description":"Extract animation data from glTF: iterate animation channels, read sampler input (timestamps) and output (T/R/S values) from buffer accessors. Store as AnimationClip with per-joint channels of keyframes. Support Linear and Step interpolation at minimum. Store rotation as quaternion, translation as vec3, scale as vec3.","kind":"task","labels":["animation"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Parse glTF animation keyframes"}	blake3:ehJQjOyGL-lXrwdzRQVfAprOg9mgz3EIzmUjfraZ4_E
1774198651347834	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjQE		item.create	bn-13y	{"description":"Add animation time tracking to ViewerState. In the render loop, interpolate keyframes at current time to get per-joint local transforms. Walk the joint hierarchy to compute world transforms. Upload updated joint palette each frame. Add continuous redraw mode (request_redraw every frame when animation is playing). Add play/pause/restart keybindings.","kind":"task","labels":["animation"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Animation playback loop and joint matrix update"}	blake3:d2AtcUrLVmxfrhGsWb4OFlu0Wzx70RxHJaNy-DIDcJM
1774198653858829	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjgE		item.create	bn-3k7	{"description":"Implement or integrate a BVH parser: read HIERARCHY section (joint names, offsets, channel order) and MOTION section (frame count, frame time, per-frame channel values). Produce a BvhClip struct with skeleton hierarchy and per-frame joint rotations/positions. Add .bvh to the supported file extensions in CLI argument handling.","kind":"task","labels":["bvh"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"BVH file parser"}	blake3:KoRnPK_wXy_TveXm9pZlf4_wwlfBw02BMNda8AI8ud4
1774198657320439	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjwE		item.create	bn-16d	{"description":"Map BVH joint hierarchy onto a loaded glTF skeleton. MVP: match by joint name (case-insensitive). Apply BVH frame data as local joint rotations, converting from BVH Euler angles (with channel order) to quaternions. Feed into the same animation playback pipeline as glTF animations. Handle rest-pose differences between BVH T-pose and glTF bind pose.","kind":"task","labels":["bvh"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"l","title":"BVH-to-skeleton mapping and playback"}	blake3:YFYwKoWIcmB1Putc3kaLv7fEd5qhCQtvYZtawzEtl2I
