1774203525812792	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtrwE		item.create	bn-3dq	{"description":"Render BVH motion capture files as animated stick figures without requiring a mesh. When `msh view foo.bvh` is invoked, display the skeleton as lines (bones) and points (joints) using forward kinematics.\n\nRequires:\n- Forward kinematics: compute world-space joint positions per frame from BVH hierarchy (OFFSET + rotation channels). T_world = T_parent * Translate(offset) * R_local\n- Euler-to-quaternion: reuse euler_to_quat from bvh_mapping.rs\n- Line rendering: draw lines between parent-child joints. Can reuse the wireframe pipeline or add a simple line primitive.\n- Joint points: optional, small spheres or just rely on line endpoints\n- Animation: wire into existing AnimationState for playback controls (Space, [, ])\n- Camera: auto-fit to skeleton bounding box\n\nEntry point: when `msh view foo.bvh` is called (no --bvh flag, the file itself is .bvh), switch to skeleton visualization mode instead of printing a summary.\n\nThis sidesteps the retargeting problem entirely — the BVH plays back on its own skeleton.","kind":"task","labels":["bvh","visualization"],"parent":"bn-1s8","size":"m","title":"Standalone BVH skeleton visualization"}	blake3:9nbqzyKfdqsB02IdAW-JnAyjkj6tHYBYpdPM8c_nnrA
1774204121422344	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtsAE		item.move	bn-3dq	{"state":"done"}	blake3:v1oNye2muax1RlzOlYj42UZxmTxvzk4t-t2R0NAR-xs
1774204977821219	command-lattice-dev	itc:v3:AWKTkyTOeZ5M5QAAAAAAQa61bvb1ugAAAAEvDQ		item.create	bn-30a	{"description":"Add animation support to 'msh render' for generating sprite sheets from animated GLB files.\n\nContext: The command-lattice project has an AI asset pipeline that generates rigged, animated GLB models (text → image → TRELLIS mesh → UniRig skeleton → MoMask/procedural animation). The final step is rendering these to isometric sprite sheets for the 2D game client (SC1-style).\n\nRequired features:\n- Read and evaluate GLB skeletal animation keyframes (the skeleton/skinning loader already exists)\n- --frame <N> to render a specific animation frame\n- --frames <start>-<end> to render a range\n- --sprite-sheet to compose multiple frames into a single atlas PNG\n- --angles <N> to render from N evenly-spaced yaw rotations (e.g. 8 for 8-directional sprites)\n- Combine with existing --preset sprite-bake, --transparent-bg, --projection ortho\n\nOutput: a single PNG atlas with rows=angles, cols=frames (or configurable layout). This replaces the current manual Blender rendering step.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- msh render model.glb --animation idle --frames 0-15 --angles 8 --sprite-sheet --out idle_sheet.png produces a usable sprite atlas\n- Works with the existing skeleton/skinning system (BVH playback not required, just GLB embedded animations)\n- Transparent background support for compositing","kind":"task","title":"Animated sprite sheet rendering"}	blake3:VYRg6FSYx_g07lCwu8uooji1gIhBrbbjiDGb-33N2YA
1774205340696342	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtsQE		item.update	bn-30a	{"field":"kind","value":"goal"}	blake3:62knDsO86W8GvjZBrt8VVlhl926okQnq6bZydagxeTk
1774205377209380	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtsgE		item.create	bn-1fo	{"description":"Extend headless.rs render_to_file() to support rendering a specific animation frame.\n\nAdd parameters:\n- animation_index: Option<usize> — which animation clip to use\n- animation_time: Option<f32> — time in seconds to evaluate\n\nWhen both are provided:\n1. Load mesh with skeleton and animations (already done by existing loader)\n2. Evaluate the animation at the given time using sample_channel + compose_trs (from animation.rs)\n3. Compute joint matrices with compute_joint_matrices_with_pose\n4. Upload to joint palette before rendering\n\nFactor out the animation evaluation logic from render.rs's RedrawRequested handler into a reusable function (e.g. in animation.rs) so both interactive and headless can call it.","kind":"task","labels":["rendering"],"parent":"bn-30a","size":"m","title":"Headless animation frame rendering"}	blake3:ugmsV7ADEvMTKHvnS6R8Crn1iX7Hk54ZX40lurmHDOs
1774205377367985	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtswE		item.create	bn-3e8	{"description":"Add --angles <N> flag to the Render command to render the model from N evenly-spaced yaw rotations around the Y axis.\n\nWhen --angles 8 is given:\n- Render at 0°, 45°, 90°, 135°, 180°, 225°, 270°, 315°\n- Each render uses the same camera distance/elevation but rotated around the model\n- Output N separate images (model_000.png, model_045.png, etc.) OR feed into the sprite sheet compositor\n\nThe rotation should be applied to the model matrix (not the camera), so the lighting stays consistent across angles.","kind":"task","labels":["rendering"],"parent":"bn-30a","size":"m","title":"Multi-angle rendering"}	blake3:NP03859cy1dpq5R4qSaOphVPe3UG8DWGKm5GTupFIJ0
1774205377524787	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEttAE		item.create	bn-3a1	{"description":"Add --sprite-sheet flag to compose multiple rendered frames into a single atlas PNG.\n\nLayout: rows = angles, cols = frames (configurable with --layout rows-first or cols-first).\n\nImplementation:\n- Render all (angle × frame) combinations to individual RGBA buffers in memory\n- Composite into a single image: tile_width * num_cols × tile_height * num_rows\n- Use the image crate (already a dependency) for the final PNG save\n- Support --transparent-bg for compositing-ready output\n\nExample: --frames 0-15 --angles 8 produces 8 rows × 16 cols = 128 tiles","kind":"task","labels":["rendering"],"parent":"bn-30a","size":"m","title":"Sprite sheet atlas compositor"}	blake3:ILBujObDw0fzHPGSIcoq70nz0KEFdWZxRXTy8GNBbCo
1774205377700543	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEttQE		item.create	bn-1es	{"description":"Wire the new flags into the Render command in main.rs:\n\nNew CLI args:\n- --animation <name-or-index>: select animation clip by name or index (default: first)\n- --frame <N>: render a single animation frame (by frame number, converted to time via duration/frame_count)\n- --frames <start>-<end>: render a range of frames\n- --angles <N>: number of rotation angles (default: 1, no rotation)\n- --sprite-sheet: compose output into a single atlas PNG instead of individual files\n- --layout <rows-first|cols-first>: atlas layout (default: rows=angles, cols=frames)\n\nIntegration: orchestrate the render loop — for each angle × frame, call the headless renderer, collect results, optionally composite into atlas.","kind":"task","labels":["cli"],"parent":"bn-30a","size":"s","title":"CLI args and integration for sprite sheet pipeline"}	blake3:UndaMW6pEk6FxrrtX8O2u8LJgi2PW8OeSAHs7VBDW20
1774205382974086	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEttgE		item.link	bn-3e8	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-1fo"}	blake3:q1OLrar8OZQc8xGm-ioVixoNvZXRLvxGLph1IVJnPuY
