1774968815546713	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtgwI		item.comment	bn-t2u	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nLocation: src/mesh/writer.rs (new file)\n\nWrite a GLB file from mesh data. The gltf crate (1.4.1, already a dependency) is primarily a reader — for writing we'll need gltf-json to build the JSON structure and pack binary buffers manually.\n\nCore function:\n  pub fn write_glb(\n      path: &PathBuf,\n      positions: &[[f32; 3]],\n      face_indices: &[[u32; 3]],\n      normals: Option<&[[f32; 3]]>,\n      face_colors: Option<&[[f32; 4]]>,    // per-face RGBA\n      texcoords: Option<&[[f32; 2]]>,\n      texture: Option<&TextureData>,        // RGBA pixels + dimensions\n  ) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>\n\nGLB binary format (spec: registry.khronos.org/glTF/specs/2.0):\n1. 12-byte header: magic (0x46546C67), version (2), total length\n2. JSON chunk: gltf-json document describing accessors, buffer views, materials\n3. BIN chunk: packed vertex positions, normals, indices, UVs, colors\n\nBuilding the JSON document with gltf-json:\n- 1 scene, 1 node, 1 mesh with 1 primitive\n- Buffer views: positions (VEC3 f32), normals (VEC3 f32), indices (SCALAR u32), optionally UVs (VEC2 f32) and colors (VEC4 f32)\n- If texture provided: embed PNG as image, create sampler + texture + material with baseColorTexture\n- If face_colors provided but no texture: use material baseColorFactor for uniform color, or vertex colors for per-face\n- Compute min/max for position accessor (required by spec)\n\nEstimated size: 200-350 lines.\n\nCheck if gltf-json is already pulled in as a transitive dep of gltf crate (it usually is).\nIf not, add gltf-json to Cargo.toml.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Writes valid GLB that loads in Blender, meshlab, and msh view\n- [ ] Positions and face indices roundtrip correctly (load GLB -> write GLB -> load again: same geometry)\n- [ ] Per-face colors preserved in output when present\n- [ ] Texture + UV coordinates preserved when present\n- [ ] Normals computed and included (auto-generate smooth normals from geometry if not provided)\n- [ ] Output file is spec-compliant GLB v2 (passes glTF-Validator)\n- [ ] Handles meshes from 8 verts (cube) to 100K+ verts without issues"}	blake3:J9Tzh9MrifOUkEjRVv01XPQNOr7zmFXKcGvbLv8ZWhc
1774968815563540	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthAI		item.comment	bn-156	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nLocation: src/mesh/writer.rs (add dispatch fn) + src/mesh/processing.rs (replace write_to_file calls)\n\nAdd a format-dispatching write function:\n  pub fn write_mesh(\n      path: &PathBuf,\n      mesh: &CornerTableF,         // for OBJ output (baby_shark write_to_file)\n      mesh_data: Option<&MeshWithColors>,  // for GLB output (preserves materials/textures)\n  ) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>\n\nLogic:\n  match path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()).map(|s| s.to_lowercase()) {\n      Some(\"obj\") => baby_shark write_to_file,\n      Some(\"glb\") => write_glb(...),\n      Some(\"gltf\") => write_gltf_separate(...),  // JSON + separate .bin\n      _ => error(\"unsupported output format\"),\n  }\n\nThen replace all 6 write_to_file calls in processing.rs with write_mesh.\nAlso update the manual OBJ write in the remesh project CLI handler (main.rs).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] 'msh remesh simplify input.glb -o output.glb' writes GLB\n- [ ] 'msh remesh simplify input.glb -o output.obj' writes OBJ (existing behavior)\n- [ ] 'msh fix input.obj -o output.glb' writes GLB\n- [ ] Unsupported extension (e.g. .stl) gives clear error message\n- [ ] All existing commands that write output respect the new dispatch\n- [ ] No behavior change when output is .obj (backward compatible)"}	blake3:pKLWehNKFX4lLu_kpynVIA0xF8bZ9SSGvgjAmSTHJf0
1774968815581537	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthQI		item.comment	bn-32c	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nCurrently, remesh operations go through CornerTableF which loses material/color/texture data.\nThe pipeline is: load MeshWithColors -> to_corner_table -> process -> write_to_file (OBJ only).\n\nFor GLB output to preserve materials, we need to carry MeshWithColors metadata alongside the CornerTableF during processing, or reconstruct it after.\n\nOptions:\nA) Thread MeshWithColors through processing functions (invasive, touches every fn signature)\nB) After processing CornerTableF, rebuild MeshWithColors from the processed mesh + original metadata\n   - Extract positions and face indices from processed CornerTableF\n   - Nearest-vertex mapping to transfer per-vertex colors/UVs from original\n   - Keep original texture/material data unchanged\n\nOption B is simpler and works for our case:\n  pub fn transfer_attributes(\n      original: &MeshWithColors,\n      processed_positions: &[[f32; 3]],\n      processed_faces: &[[u32; 3]],\n  ) -> MeshWithColors\n\nFor each vertex in the processed mesh, find the nearest vertex in the original mesh\nand copy its UV coordinates, joint weights, etc. Colors can be transferred per-face\nby finding the original face that best overlaps each new face.\n\nEstimated size: 100-200 lines.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Load colored GLB -> remesh voxel -> write GLB: colors approximately preserved\n- [ ] Load textured GLB -> simplify -> write GLB: UVs transferred to nearest original vertex\n- [ ] Pipeline without color data still works (no regression on plain geometry)\n- [ ] Attribute transfer completes in <100ms for 4K vertex meshes"}	blake3:HpAtylSECkPm2F4kAol1rJElyIyVy2N3GEFD0zM5hLk
1774968815598646	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthgI		item.comment	bn-1em	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nEnd-to-end validation of the full roundtrip.\n\nTest cases:\n1. Plain geometry: cube.glb -> remesh voxel -> simplify -> write cube_out.glb -> load and verify\n2. Colored mesh: colored.glb -> simplify -> write colored_out.glb -> verify colors present\n3. Textured mesh: textured.glb -> simplify -> write textured_out.glb -> verify texture + UVs\n4. Cross-format: input.glb -> remesh -> output.obj (and vice versa: input.obj -> output.glb)\n5. Full cleanup pipeline: input.glb -> clean -> output.glb\n\nValidation methods:\n- Load output in msh view, visual inspection\n- Load in Blender, check material/texture preservation\n- Compare vertex counts and bounding boxes\n- Run glTF-Validator on output files\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] At least 3 GLB test meshes roundtripped successfully\n- [ ] Cross-format conversion (OBJ->GLB, GLB->OBJ) works\n- [ ] glTF-Validator reports no errors on output\n- [ ] Visual inspection confirms no obvious geometry or material degradation\n- [ ] Document any known limitations (e.g. multi-material, skinned meshes)"}	blake3:BKLmIlqrYxg5aRf4UOe496qXNsBYspszOl2aneJ1Cd0
1774968854352432	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEthwI		item.comment	bn-3mg	{"body":"## Test models\n\nUse GLB models from ~/src/command-lattice/ws/default/assets/models/. Good representative set:\n\nBuildings (static, sharp edges):\n- barracks.glb, depot.glb, factory.glb, hq.glb, refinery.glb\n\nResources (organic, smooth):\n- mineral.glb, geyser.glb\n\nUnits (rigged, low-poly):\n- rifleman.glb, scout.glb, worker.glb\n\nRun msh stats on each to get baseline vertex/face counts, then test the pipeline on 2-3 from each category."}	blake3:TD6r72zDnEf9h08Gi7XBBt9z3TzbnGlckExuvEJuJUI
1774968854376367	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtiAI		item.comment	bn-1em	{"body":"## Test models\n\nUse GLB models from ~/src/command-lattice/ws/default/assets/models/ for roundtrip testing. These are the actual game assets the pipeline will process."}	blake3:N98oOd4O9035VLVY3xfTRNCfe5nMo2fbGnFpOAS0qW0
