1774970779650617	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjgI		item.comment	bn-1nh	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nReplace the heuristic iterative projection (project_to_reference in projection.rs) with del-* crate solver.\n\nAdd dependencies to Cargo.toml:\n  del-msh-core, del-geo-core, del-fem-core (for future Tier 2)\n\nNew function in projection.rs:\n  pub fn project_with_solver(\n      positions: &mut [na::Point3<f32>],\n      triangles: &[[u32; 3]],\n      reference_grid: &SpatialHashGrid,\n      config: &ProjectionConfig,\n  ) -> ProjectionStats\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute goal positions: for each vertex, find closest point on reference mesh via SpatialHashGrid\n2. Convert to flat f64 arrays (del-msh-core uses &[f64] flat stride-3)\n3. Convert triangles to &[usize] flat stride-3\n4. Call del_msh_core::trimesh3_move_avoid_intersection::match_vtx2xyz_while_avoid_collision(\n       &tri2vtx, &current_positions_f64, &goal_positions_f64,\n       Params { k_diff: 1.0, k_contact: 100.0, dist0: 0.01, alpha: 0.1, num_iter: 50 }\n   )\n5. Convert result back to Point3<f32>\n\nAlso update the CLI handler in main.rs to call the new function instead of project_to_reference.\n\nKeep the old heuristic function available behind a --legacy flag or remove it.\n\nData format conversion notes:\n- del-msh uses flat &[f64] for positions (stride 3) and flat &[usize] for triangles (stride 3)\n- Our code uses Vec<na::Point3<f32>> and Vec<[u32; 3]>\n- Need f32->f64 conversion since match_vtx2xyz_while_avoid_collision is f64-only\n\nThe match_vtx2xyz_while_avoid_collision function internally:\n- Asserts start mesh has no self-intersections\n- Builds edge connectivity\n- Iterative gradient descent with barrier energy for proximity\n- CCD line search for safe step size\n- Backtracking to ensure energy decrease\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] del-msh-core and del-geo-core added to Cargo.toml and compile\n- [ ] 'msh remesh project' uses the del-* solver by default\n- [ ] Barracks, rifleman, mineral pipelines produce visually better results than heuristic\n- [ ] No self-intersections in output (verified by del-msh trimesh3_intersection)\n- [ ] Projection completes in <5 seconds for 2K vertex mesh\n- [ ] Max displacement outliers (like rifleman's 0.38) are eliminated\n- [ ] Stats still reported (displacement, iterations)"}	blake3:XwkLC3I5uNywgEk3pfOwd2fKZcKVIHzF_7f_hjQVmpA
1774970779668927	msh-dev	itc:v3:AWLzMzyc5k_JEAAAAAAAQfbb13a_UAAAAAEtjwI		item.comment	bn-1ka	{"body":"## Implementation details\n\nFull Newton-CG solver using del-fem-core energy terms + del-ls sparse solver.\nOnly implement if Tier 1 quality is insufficient.\n\nEnergy functional:\n  E = w_dist * E_distance + w_elas * E_elastic + w_bend * E_bending\n\nComponents:\n- E_distance: quadratic pull toward reference surface (from goal positions via spatial hash)\n  Gradient: 2 * w_dist * (x - target), Hessian: 2 * w_dist * I (diagonal)\n- E_elastic: del_fem_core::stvk_tri3::wdwddw_() per triangle\n  Returns energy + gradient + 9x9 Hessian per element\n- E_bending: del_fem_core::quadratic_bending::wdw() per interior edge\n  Constant Hessian (precomputable from rest shape)\n\nSolver loop:\n1. Build sparsity pattern from mesh topology (3*V scalar DOFs)\n2. Initialize del_ls::linearsystem::Solver\n3. For each Newton iteration:\n   a. solver.begin_merge()\n   b. Assemble distance energy Hessian (diagonal)\n   c. For each triangle: compute StVK wdwddw_, merge 9x9 Hessian + gradient\n   d. For each hinge: compute quadratic_bending, merge 12x12 Hessian + gradient\n   e. solver.end_merge() (ILU factorization)\n   f. solver.solve_pcg()\n   g. CCD line search using del_geo_core::ccd3\n   h. Update positions\n4. Check convergence (gradient norm < epsilon)\n\nEstimated size: 400-600 lines.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Newton solver converges in <20 iterations for test meshes\n- [ ] Sharp edges better preserved than Tier 1 (hinge energy)\n- [ ] Triangle quality maintained (elastic energy prevents inversion)\n- [ ] Hausdorff distance to original < Tier 1 result\n- [ ] Completes in <10 seconds for 2K vertex mesh"}	blake3:f_-KkTizj0X5cIGxsG2Szhp9AYsKO--XgYYhVmBKJXE
